<title>BRAZIL: Brazil CSN chief to tender resignation.</title>
<headline>Brazil CSN chief to tender resignation.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of Brazilian steel company Companhia Siderurgica Nacional (CSN), Sylvio Coutinho, is meeting with the firm's board of directors to hand in his resignation, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman would not comment any further, saying CSN would make a statement after the meeting which is being held in Sao Paulo.</p>
<p>-- Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151</p>
</text>
